doc:sec-41cb-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41CB(3) Medical device standards" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order under subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order, may make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time." ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41CC Content of medical device standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41cc ;
    values:originalText "(1) Without limiting the scope of section 41CB, an order establishing a medical device standard for kinds of medical devices may be specified by reference to: (a) the safety or performance characteristics of the devices; or (b) a monograph in the British Pharmacopoeia, the European Pharmacopoeia or the United States Pharmacopeia-National Formulary; or (c) a monograph in a publication approved by the Minister for the purposes of this subsection; or  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Essential principles and medical device standards  Part 4-2 Medical device standards  Division 2 Section 41CD Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (d) such a monograph as modified in a manner specified in the order; or (e) a standard published by a standards organisation; or (f) such other matters as the Minister thinks fit. (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), these are standards organisations: (a) Standards Australia; (b) the International Organisation for Standardization; (c) the International Electrotechnical Commission; (d) the European Committee for Standardization; (e) the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization; (f) any other organisation declared by the Minister by notice published in the Gazette or on the Department’s website." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Without limiting the scope of section 41CB, an order establishing a medical device standard for kinds of medical devices may be specified by reference to: (a) the safety or performance characteristics of the devices; or (b) a monograph in the British Pharmacopoeia, the European Pharmacopoeia or the United States Pharmacopeia-National Formulary; or (c) a monograph in a publication approved by the Minister for the purposes of this subsection; or  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Essential principles and medical device standards  Part 4-2 Medical device standards  Division 2 Section 41CD Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (d) such a monograph as modified in a manner specified in the order; or (e) a standard published by a standards organisation; or (f) such other matters as the Minister thinks fit. (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(e), these are standards organisations: (a) Standards Australia; (b) the International Organisation for Standardization; (c) the International Electrotechnical Commission; (d) the European Committee for Standardization; (e) the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization; (f) any other organisation declared by the Minister by notice published in the Gazette or on the Department’s website."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "403f3edb1aec87783a330def66040ac8959deb96319b85789f6d76910162b2eb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cc-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cc-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
