concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41D What this Part is about"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41d ;
    values:originalText "The conformity assessment procedures set out the requirements relating to the application of quality management systems for medical devices, and other requirements imposed on manufacturers. Compliance with applicable conformity assessment standards is not required, but it is one way to establish that one or more parts of the conformity assessment procedures have been applied to medical devices. Note 1: Dealing in medical devices that have not had the conformity assessment procedures applied may be an offence or may contravene a civil penalty provision: see Division 2 of Part 4-11. Note 2: See section 41BI on applying the conformity assessment procedures.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Conformity assessment procedures  Part 4-3 Conformity assessment procedures  Division 1 Section 41DA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    skos:definition "The conformity assessment procedures set out the requirements relating to the application of quality management systems for medical devices, and other requirements imposed on manufacturers. Compliance with applicable conformity assessment standards is not required, but it is one way to establish that one or more parts of the conformity assessment procedures have been applied to medical devices. Note 1: Dealing in medical devices that have not had the conformity assessment procedures applied may be an offence or may contravene a civil penalty provision: see Division 2 of Part 4-11. Note 2: See section 41BI on applying the conformity assessment procedures.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Conformity assessment procedures  Part 4-3 Conformity assessment procedures  Division 1 Section 41DA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f2d950a4a205a25ba2345c7ec89d5e533df4c8d0b95edeaa02de9fbe8ef6566f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Compliance with applicable conformity assessment standards is not required, but it is one way to establish that one or more parts of the conformity assessment procedures have been applied." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.38" ;
