doc:sec-41er a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41ER Automatic revocation of conformity assessment certificates" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in relation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, revoke the certificate if: (a) the certificate has been suspended under section 41EM; and (b) the period applying to the suspension under subsection 41EM(3) or 41EO(3) (as the case requires) expires before the suspension is revoked under section 41EP." ;
    cof:pageNumber "61"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41ES Immediate revocation of conformity assessment certificates"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41es ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in relation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, revoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the revocation of the certificate. (2) If: (a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and (b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day the certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in writing, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and (c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee (if any); the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer, withdraw the revocation. (3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to have occurred.  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in relation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, revoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the revocation of the certificate. (2) If: (a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and (b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day the certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in writing, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and (c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee (if any); the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer, withdraw the revocation. (3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to have occurred.  Chapter 4  Medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f017e3a21dc97f41aad2a8c9a48226fcf5935578016a140bfe5a6c02efde8a93" ;
    cof:pageNumber "61"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.61" .
doc:sec-41es a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41ES Immediate revocation of conformity assessment certificates" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in relation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, revoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the revocation of the certificate. (2) If: (a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and (b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day the certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in writing, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and (c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee (if any); the Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer, withdraw the revocation. (3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to have occurred.  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "61"^^xsd:integer .

