concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4 cml:asserts concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1 .
concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "necessity" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Necessity condition for variation or revocation." ;
    cml:premiseText "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect: (a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the variation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the variation or revocation is made;" ;
    cml:conclusionText "The variation or revocation must be necessary to prevent imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4 cml:asserts concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2 .
concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "possibility" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Possibility condition for variation or revocation." ;
    cml:premiseText "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect: (b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or revocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the day the variation or revocation is made)." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The variation or revocation may occur on a later day." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-41gu-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41GU(4) Variation or revocation of exemption" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect: (a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the variation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the variation or revocation is made; or (b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or revocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the day the variation or revocation is made). 41GV  Informing persons of exemption etc. If the Minister makes an exemption under section 41GS, the Minister must take reasonable steps to give a copy of the following to each person covered by paragraph 41GT(c):  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41GW Notification and tabling"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41gw ;
    values:originalText "Notification (1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the following: (a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); (b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent that the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); to be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day on which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply with this subsection. Tabling (2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the following: (a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); (b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent that the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); to be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days of that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply with this subsection.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Exempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A  Section 41GY Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    skos:definition "Notification (1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the following: (a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); (b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent that the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); to be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day on which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply with this subsection. Tabling (2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the following: (a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); (b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent that the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made under section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii); to be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days of that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply with this subsection.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Exempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A  Section 41GY Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7d31b83313991d4c969b95ff28385ff891514dbe7a93c93c5db8145ad031420f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "112"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-2 ;
