doc:sec-41jd a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41JD Secretary may require information etc. about devices" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "exempted under section 41HA from inclusion in the Register (1) The Secretary may give the sponsor of kinds of medical devices exempted under subsection 41HA(1) from Division 3 of Part 4-11,  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "133"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41je a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41JE Secretary may require information relating to approvals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41je ;
    values:originalText "under section 41HB Approval under subsection 41HB(1) (1) The Secretary may give to a person granted an approval under subsection 41HB(1) (special and experimental uses), in relation to specified kinds of medical devices, a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to one or more of the following: (a) the supply of devices of those kinds; (b) the handling of devices of those kinds; (c) the monitoring of the supply of devices of those kinds; (d) the results of the supply of devices of those kinds; (e) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Approval under subsection 41HB(1)—use by another person (2) The Secretary may give to a person using specified kinds of medical devices, that are the subject of an approval granted to someone else under paragraph 41HB(1)(e) (use solely for experimental purposes in humans), a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to either of both of the following: (a) the use of devices of those kinds; (b) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Compliance period (3) A notice under this section must specify a reasonable period within which the person to whom the notice is given must comply. The period must be at least 10 working days starting on the day on which the notice is given.  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "under section 41HB Approval under subsection 41HB(1) (1) The Secretary may give to a person granted an approval under subsection 41HB(1) (special and experimental uses), in relation to specified kinds of medical devices, a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to one or more of the following: (a) the supply of devices of those kinds; (b) the handling of devices of those kinds; (c) the monitoring of the supply of devices of those kinds; (d) the results of the supply of devices of those kinds; (e) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Approval under subsection 41HB(1)—use by another person (2) The Secretary may give to a person using specified kinds of medical devices, that are the subject of an approval granted to someone else under paragraph 41HB(1)(e) (use solely for experimental purposes in humans), a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to either of both of the following: (a) the use of devices of those kinds; (b) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Compliance period (3) A notice under this section must specify a reasonable period within which the person to whom the notice is given must comply. The period must be at least 10 working days starting on the day on which the notice is given.  Chapter 4  Medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c55a6b7d2e4809fd866285fa0881f23ce036e8f46a84be94fefbd2c774940867" ;
    cof:pageNumber "135"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41je-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41je-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41je-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.135" .
doc:sec-41je a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41JE Secretary may require information relating to approvals" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "under section 41HB Approval under subsection 41HB(1) (1) The Secretary may give to a person granted an approval under subsection 41HB(1) (special and experimental uses), in relation to specified kinds of medical devices, a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to one or more of the following: (a) the supply of devices of those kinds; (b) the handling of devices of those kinds; (c) the monitoring of the supply of devices of those kinds; (d) the results of the supply of devices of those kinds; (e) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Approval under subsection 41HB(1)—use by another person (2) The Secretary may give to a person using specified kinds of medical devices, that are the subject of an approval granted to someone else under paragraph 41HB(1)(e) (use solely for experimental purposes in humans), a written notice requiring the person to give to the Secretary specified information or documents relating to either of both of the following: (a) the use of devices of those kinds; (b) any other matter prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph in relation to devices of those kinds. Compliance period (3) A notice under this section must specify a reasonable period within which the person to whom the notice is given must comply. The period must be at least 10 working days starting on the day on which the notice is given.  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    cof:pageNumber "135"^^xsd:integer .

