doc:sec-41jl a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41JL Purposes of this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The purposes of this Part are to facilitate the following: (a) monitoring and enforcing compliance with the requirements of this Chapter; (b) monitoring the safety and performance of medical devices; (c) any activities that are incidental to the above purposes.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Mandatory reporting of adverse events by healthcare facilities  Part 4-8A Mandatory reporting of adverse events  Division 2 Section 41JM Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jm a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41JM Requirement to report adverse events involving reportable"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41jm ;
    values:originalText "medical devices Report to be given to the Secretary (1) The chief executive officer (however described) of a healthcare facility must give a report to the Secretary if subsection (2), (3) or (4) applies to the healthcare facility in relation to a reportable medical device and a person. (2) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a reportable medical device is used in the facility; and (b) the use of the device has resulted in the death, or a serious deterioration in the health, of a person while the device is used in the facility. (3) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a reportable medical device is not used in the facility because of the intervention of a person in the facility; and (b) the use of the device, if the device were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, the death, or a serious deterioration in the health, of a person. (4) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a health practitioner provides treatment to a person in the facility for a serious deterioration in the health of the person; and (b) the use of a reportable medical device has resulted in the serious deterioration in the health of the person. Report requirements (5) The report must include the following information about the reportable medical device and the person: (a) the name, or a description, of the reportable medical device;  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "medical devices Report to be given to the Secretary (1) The chief executive officer (however described) of a healthcare facility must give a report to the Secretary if subsection (2), (3) or (4) applies to the healthcare facility in relation to a reportable medical device and a person. (2) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a reportable medical device is used in the facility; and (b) the use of the device has resulted in the death, or a serious deterioration in the health, of a person while the device is used in the facility. (3) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a reportable medical device is not used in the facility because of the intervention of a person in the facility; and (b) the use of the device, if the device were used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, the death, or a serious deterioration in the health, of a person. (4) This subsection applies to a healthcare facility if: (a) a health practitioner provides treatment to a person in the facility for a serious deterioration in the health of the person; and (b) the use of a reportable medical device has resulted in the serious deterioration in the health of the person. Report requirements (5) The report must include the following information about the reportable medical device and the person: (a) the name, or a description, of the reportable medical device;  Chapter 4  Medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c7820f15095fdca0e414146498540963260052da1c71f604998c30a2bc392f52" ;
    cof:pageNumber "143"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jm-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jm-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jm-ss-2 ;
