doc:sec-41kc-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41KC(1) Criminal offences for failing to comply with requirements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the person under section 41KA; and (c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. Note 1: A jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and may convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead: see section 53A. Note 2: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA." ;
    cof:pageNumber "149"^^xsd:integer .

