concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41MH Criminal offence for making false statements in declarations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41mh ;
    values:originalText "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a declaration, relating to the application of conformity assessment procedures, or the application of requirements comparable to those procedures, to a medical device that the person has manufactured; and (b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11 Failure to apply conformity assessment procedures  Division 2 Section 41MHA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. 41MHA  Civil penalty for making false statements in declarations A person contravenes this section if: (a) the person manufactures a medical device; and (b) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a declaration relating to the application of conformity assessment procedures, or the application of requirements comparable to those procedures, to the device; and (c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular. Maximum civil penalty: (a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and (b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a declaration, relating to the application of conformity assessment procedures, or the application of requirements comparable to those procedures, to a medical device that the person has manufactured; and (b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11 Failure to apply conformity assessment procedures  Division 2 Section 41MHA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. 41MHA  Civil penalty for making false statements in declarations A person contravenes this section if: (a) the person manufactures a medical device; and (b) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a declaration relating to the application of conformity assessment procedures, or the application of requirements comparable to those procedures, to the device; and (c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular. Maximum civil penalty: (a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and (b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.  Chapter 4  Medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a64bffa7442bdd9fc7ed83bf732c2ce641760dac5eef034050dbfe9a9944505" ;
    cof:pageNumber "170"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Making false statements in declarations is a criminal offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.170" ;
