doc:sec-41mo-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41MO(4) Criminal offences for misusing medical devices exempted for" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A person commits an offence if:  Medical devices  Chapter 4 Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11 Other offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4 Section 41MO Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (a) the person has been granted an authority under subsection 41HC(1) relating to a specified kind of medical device; and (b) the person supplies a medical device of that kind: (i) otherwise than in accordance with the authority; or (ii) otherwise than in accordance with any conditions to which the authority is subject; or (iii) otherwise than in accordance with any regulations made for the purpose of subsection 41HC(5). Penalty: 500 penalty units. (4AA) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person has been granted an authority under subsection 41HC(1) relating to a specified kind of medical device; and (b) the person supplies a medical device of that kind: (i) otherwise than in accordance with the authority; or (ii) otherwise than in accordance with any conditions to which the authority is subject; or (iii) otherwise than in accordance with any regulations made for the purpose of subsection 41HC(5). Penalty: 100 penalty units. (4AB) An offence against subsection (4AA) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    cof:pageNumber "190"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mo-ss-4a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41MO(4A) Criminal offences for misusing medical devices exempted for"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41mo-ss-4a ;
    values:originalText "(4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is a health practitioner; and (b) the person is included in a class of health practitioners specified in subsection 41HC(6) rules; and (c) the person supplies a medical device of a kind specified in those rules; and (d) any of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with those rules;  Chapter 4  Medical devices" ;
    skos:definition "(4A) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is a health practitioner; and (b) the person is included in a class of health practitioners specified in subsection 41HC(6) rules; and (c) the person supplies a medical device of a kind specified in those rules; and (d) any of the following applies: (i) the supply is not in accordance with those rules;  Chapter 4  Medical devices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "21b8fea6cbba4689a10e6460ef625d0a83a38d750d99b5d1ebf6422d1b711cc0" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mo ;
    cof:pageNumber "190"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Misusing medical devices is prohibited for specified health practitioners." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
