doc:sec-41q-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "41Q(4) Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate contravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping goods imported by the person into Australia. Note: For unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1).  Vaping goods  Chapter 4A Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2 General  Division 1 Section 41QA Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Exception" ;
    cof:pageNumber "204"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41Q(5) Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41q-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping goods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901. Note: The person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and section 41QE of this Act." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping goods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901. Note: The person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and section 41QE of this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ff7804e1eec2aa6b8c27ad54cbf802a47f7aecc87ee1760be2a4911e649fa44a" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q ;
    cof:pageNumber "204"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exemptions from subsections (1) to (4)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
