concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41QB Offences and civil penalty provision—supplying vaping goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41qb ;
    values:originalText "Offences (1) A person commits an offence if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. (2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  Vaping goods  Chapter 4A Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2 General  Division 1 Section 41QB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Civil penalty provision (3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Maximum civil penalty: (a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and (b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units. (4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate contravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping goods supplied by the person in Australia. Note: For unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1). Exceptions—general (5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if: (a) subsections (6), (7) and (8) apply in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person; or (b) subsections (9), (10) and (11) apply in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person. Note: The person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsections (6), (7) and (8) or subsections (9), (10) and (11): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and section 41QE of this Act. Exceptions—wholesale supply chain (6) This subsection applies in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person if: (a) the vaping goods are therapeutic goods that are entered on the Register; or (b) both of the following apply: (i) the vaping goods are therapeutic goods that are exempt goods under regulations made for the purposes of subsection 18(1) or an exempt device under regulations made for the purposes of subsection 41HA(1), and the sponsor has given the Secretary a notice in compliance with the exemption;  Chapter 4A  Vaping goods" ;
    skos:definition "Offences (1) A person commits an offence if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Penalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. (2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  Vaping goods  Chapter 4A Offences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2 General  Division 1 Section 41QB Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 Civil penalty provision (3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person supplies vaping goods in Australia. Maximum civil penalty: (a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and (b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units. (4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate contravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping goods supplied by the person in Australia. Note: For unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1). Exceptions—general (5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if: (a) subsections (6), (7) and (8) apply in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person; or (b) subsections (9), (10) and (11) apply in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person. Note: The person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsections (6), (7) and (8) or subsections (9), (10) and (11): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and section 41QE of this Act. Exceptions—wholesale supply chain (6) This subsection applies in relation to the supply of the vaping goods by the person if: (a) the vaping goods are therapeutic goods that are entered on the Register; or (b) both of the following apply: (i) the vaping goods are therapeutic goods that are exempt goods under regulations made for the purposes of subsection 18(1) or an exempt device under regulations made for the purposes of subsection 41HA(1), and the sponsor has given the Secretary a"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "87d390231948a0c49033f78db1046b1c0ea049452008ec1792ea0a263799dcc6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "206"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qb-ss-6 ;
