    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and (b) the act or omission breaches a condition of a consent imposed under subsection 41RC(2); and (c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person. Penalty: 2,000 penalty units. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA." ;
    cof:pageNumber "224"^^xsd:integer .

