doc:sec-42dl a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42DL Advertising offences—general" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) subsection (5), (6), (7), (8), (9), (10), (11) or (12) applies to the advertisement; and (c) either:  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering" ;
    cof:pageNumber "235"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42DM Offences—non-compliance with the Therapeutic Goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42dm ;
    values:originalText "Advertising Code (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code; and (c) either: (i) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement, if the goods were so used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering" ;
    skos:definition "Advertising Code (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code; and (c) either: (i) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement, if the goods were so used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "95bbe0b7db7e2452098f9658e3c72bad594c36f3cac2125faa72cf20730625d6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "243"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.243" .
doc:sec-42dm a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42DM Offences—non-compliance with the Therapeutic Goods" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Advertising Code (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code; and (c) either: (i) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement has resulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or (ii) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement, if the goods were so used, would result in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury to any person. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or (ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic goods; and (b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person: (i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering" ;
    cof:pageNumber "243"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
