concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42DP Offences—dissemination of generic information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42dp ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information about therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public; and (b) the dissemination of that generic information does not comply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the purposes of section 42DO. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both.  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5 Advertising and generic information  Part 5-1 Generic information about ingredients or components of therapeutic goods  Division 4 Section 42DQ Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information about therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public; and (b) the dissemination of that generic information does not comply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the purposes of section 42DO. Penalty: 100 penalty units. (3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information about therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public; and (b) the dissemination of that generic information does not comply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the purposes of section 42DO. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both.  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5 Advertising and generic information  Part 5-1 Generic information about ingredients or components of therapeutic goods  Division 4 Section 42DQ Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information about therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public; and (b) the dissemination of that generic information does not comply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods Advertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the purposes of section 42DO. Penalty: 100 penalty units. (3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "761f9fe9d7758baeb94c994517171b62534f87ab7823c519511ee2098f7854a2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "246"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.246" .
