doc:sec-42ea a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42EA Civil penalty relating to dealing with counterfeit therapeutic" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "goods A person contravenes this section if: (a) the person does any of the following: (i) manufactures goods in Australia; (ii) supplies goods in Australia; (iii) imports goods into Australia; (iv) exports goods from Australia; and (b) the goods are therapeutic goods; and (c) the goods are counterfeit. Maximum civil penalty: (a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and (b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "271"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42eb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42EB Relief from liability for certain contraventions relating to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42eb ;
    values:originalText "dealing with counterfeit therapeutic goods (1) If: (a) proceedings for the contravention of section 42EA (a civil penalty provision) are brought against a person; and (b) in the proceedings it appears to the Court that the person has, or may have, contravened that section but that: (i) the person has a reasonable excuse; and (ii) having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the person ought fairly to be excused for the contravention;  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering" ;
    skos:definition "dealing with counterfeit therapeutic goods (1) If: (a) proceedings for the contravention of section 42EA (a civil penalty provision) are brought against a person; and (b) in the proceedings it appears to the Court that the person has, or may have, contravened that section but that: (i) the person has a reasonable excuse; and (ii) having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the person ought fairly to be excused for the contravention;  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"@en ;
