doc:sec-42vb-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42VB(4) Relief from liability for contraventions relating to the recall of" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of subsection (2) as applying for the purposes of a case tried by a judge with a jury: (a) a reference in that subsection to the Court is a reference to the judge; and (b) the relief that may be granted includes withdrawing the case in whole or in part from the jury and directing judgment to be entered for the person on such terms as to costs as the judge thinks appropriate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "278"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42w a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42W Supply etc. of therapeutic goods that are subject to recall"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42w ;
    values:originalText "requirements (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person supplies therapeutic goods in Australia; and (b) either: (i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a kind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which requirements have been imposed under section 42V, on that person or another person, to recall therapeutic goods; or (ii) the therapeutic goods are of such a kind, or are included in such a batch, and the person is reckless as to that fact; and (c) the Secretary has not consented in writing to the supply. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person exports therapeutic goods from Australia; and (b) either: (i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a kind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which requirements have been imposed under section 42V, on  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering" ;
    skos:definition "requirements (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person supplies therapeutic goods in Australia; and (b) either: (i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a kind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which requirements have been imposed under section 42V, on that person or another person, to recall therapeutic goods; or (ii) the therapeutic goods are of such a kind, or are included in such a batch, and the person is reckless as to that fact; and (c) the Secretary has not consented in writing to the supply. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or both. Note: For the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see sections 54B and 54BA. (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person exports therapeutic goods from Australia; and (b) either: (i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a kind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which requirements have been imposed under section 42V, on  Chapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "10762e1094dbeeaba59c58cec8a91b71b99f2063f7f1f20e5c0e3e635f42b2df" ;
    cof:pageNumber "279"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42w-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42w-ss-2 ;
