doc:sec-42yd a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42YD Recovery of a pecuniary penalty" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If the Federal Court orders a person to pay a pecuniary penalty: (a) the penalty is payable to the Commonwealth; and (b) the Commonwealth may enforce the order as if it were a judgment of the Court." ;
    cof:pageNumber "283"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ye a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42YE Gathering information for application for pecuniary penalty"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42ye ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if it appears to the Secretary that a person (the wrongdoer) may have contravened a civil penalty provision. (2) If the Secretary, on reasonable grounds, suspects that a person other than the wrongdoer can give information relevant to an application for a civil penalty order in relation to the contravention, whether or not such an application has been made, the Secretary may, by writing given to the person, require the person to give all reasonable assistance in connection with such an application.  Chapter 5A  Enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if it appears to the Secretary that a person (the wrongdoer) may have contravened a civil penalty provision. (2) If the Secretary, on reasonable grounds, suspects that a person other than the wrongdoer can give information relevant to an application for a civil penalty order in relation to the contravention, whether or not such an application has been made, the Secretary may, by writing given to the person, require the person to give all reasonable assistance in connection with such an application.  Chapter 5A  Enforcement"@en ;
