doc:sec-42yl-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "42YL(4) Enforcement of undertakings" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Secretary considers that the person who gave the undertaking has breached any of its terms, the Secretary may apply to the Federal Court for an order under subsection (5)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "295"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42YL(5) Enforcement of undertakings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42yl-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If the Court is satisfied that the person has breached a term of the undertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following orders: (a) an order directing the person to comply with that term of the undertaking; (b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an amount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the person has obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the breach; (c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the person to compensate any other person who has suffered loss or damage as a result of the breach; (d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.  Chapter 5A  Enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "(5) If the Court is satisfied that the person has breached a term of the undertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following orders: (a) an order directing the person to comply with that term of the undertaking; (b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an amount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the person has obtained directly or indirectly and that is reasonably attributable to the breach; (c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the person to compensate any other person who has suffered loss or damage as a result of the breach; (d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.  Chapter 5A  Enforcement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "da8a864732f059b045c128da653b95f49fe84883ee6e0a3a165a9fcbec844145" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl ;
    cof:pageNumber "295"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court may make orders to enforce undertaking breach" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.295" ;
