    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Restraining injunctions (1) The power of the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under this Part to grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct may be exercised: (a) whether or not it appears to the court that the person intends to engage again, or to continue to engage, in conduct of that kind; and (b) whether or not the person has previously engaged in conduct of that kind; and (c) whether or not there is an imminent danger of substantial damage to any other person if the person engages in conduct of that kind.  Chapter 5A  Enforcement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "297"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yr a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42YR Other powers of court unaffected"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-42yr ;
    values:originalText "The powers conferred on the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under this Part are in addition to, and not instead of, any other powers of the court, whether conferred by this Act or otherwise.  Enforcement  Chapter 5A Enforceable directions  Part 5A-5  Section 42YS Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    skos:definition "The powers conferred on the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) under this Part are in addition to, and not instead of, any other powers of the court, whether conferred by this Act or otherwise.  Enforcement  Chapter 5A Enforceable directions  Part 5A-5  Section 42YS Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "321527a650447a14f5fda26e46a4d01afb7857a21f46d18d23d15b9b178ff866" ;
    cof:pageNumber "298"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court's other powers unaffected" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
