    cof:title "46 Searches to monitor compliance with Act or regulations" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), an authorised person may, for the purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations have been complied with: (a) enter any premises; and (b) exercise the powers set out in subsection 48(1) and section 48BA. (2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless: (a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or (b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 49. (3) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under subsection (1) in relation to premises if: (a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised person to produce his or her identity card for inspection by the occupier; and (b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement." ;
    cof:pageNumber "314"^^xsd:integer .

