concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48C(3) Use of electronic equipment at premises relating to offences and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-48c-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) An authorised person may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if: (a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form as mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to transfer the material as mentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or (b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute an offence." ;
    skos:definition "(3) An authorised person may seize equipment under paragraph (2)(a) only if: (a) it is not practicable to put the material in documentary form as mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) or to transfer the material as mentioned in paragraph (2)(c); or (b) possession by the occupier of the equipment could constitute an offence."@en ;
