concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48C(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises relating to offences and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-48c-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that: (a) evidential material in respect of an offence against this Act, in respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision or in respect of both may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that: (a) evidential material in respect of an offence against this Act, in respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision or in respect of both may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "752409f0bfc34fddb81506cee9e8803349c9680e9a7cc0c46570c64284085f8d" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c ;
    cof:pageNumber "324"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorized person may take necessary actions to secure electronic equipment." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.324" ;
