doc:sec-48d-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "48D(2) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament for the purpose." ;
    cof:pageNumber "326"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48D(3) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-48d-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her employees and agents, if they were available at the time, had provided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the equipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.  Administration  Chapter 6 Entry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2  Section 48E Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025" ;
    skos:definition "(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her employees and agents, if they were available at the time, had provided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the equipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.  Administration  Chapter 6 Entry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2  Section 48E Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "07285c55838625e1b42c8cf82ca617a278754a10968f319e06b6f8ef0e0243e6" ;
