concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "51C Issuing officers—personal capacity"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-51c ;
    values:originalText "Powers conferred personally (1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on the issuing officer: (a) in a personal capacity; and  Administration  Chapter 6 Entry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2  Section 52 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court. Powers need not be accepted (2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred. Protection and immunity (3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the same protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were exercising the power: (a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer; or (b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer." ;
    skos:definition "Powers conferred personally (1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on the issuing officer: (a) in a personal capacity; and  Administration  Chapter 6 Entry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2  Section 52 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court. Powers need not be accepted (2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred. Protection and immunity (3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the same protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were exercising the power: (a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer; or (b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a3d9ce38f203e8b183955c1df3c707be225fa24ea2ebd96628bb6f45dc1fcae0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "334"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf> ;
    dc:source "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.334" .
doc:sec-51c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "51C Issuing officers—personal capacity" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Powers conferred personally (1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on the issuing officer: (a) in a personal capacity; and  Administration  Chapter 6 Entry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2  Section 52 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court. Powers need not be accepted (2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred. Protection and immunity (3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the same protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were exercising the power: (a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer; or (b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an officer." ;
    cof:pageNumber "334"^^xsd:integer .

