doc:sec-52e-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "52E(1) Secretary to take certain matters into account in exercising" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In exercising a power under subsection 52D(2), the Secretary must take the following matters into account (where relevant): (a) the risks and benefits of the use of a substance; (b) the purposes for which a substance is to be used and the extent of use of a substance; (c) the toxicity of a substance; (d) the dosage, formulation, labelling, packaging and presentation of a substance; (e) the potential for abuse of a substance; (f) any other matters that the Secretary considers necessary to protect public health." ;
    cof:pageNumber "344"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "52E(2) Secretary to take certain matters into account in exercising"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-52e-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In exercising a power under subsection 52D(2), the Secretary must comply with any guidelines of: (a) the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council; and (b) the subcommittee of the Council known as the National Coordinating Committee on Therapeutic Goods (or any replacement subcommittee); notified to the Secretary for the purposes of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In exercising a power under subsection 52D(2), the Secretary must comply with any guidelines of: (a) the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council; and (b) the subcommittee of the Council known as the National Coordinating Committee on Therapeutic Goods (or any replacement subcommittee); notified to the Secretary for the purposes of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a325ddf6748881193ebf7a96606e226ea43e8432f4475d29bccfab32ae2e9a10" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52e ;
    cof:pageNumber "344"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application requirements Secretary must comply with guidelines from the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council and the National Coordinating Committee on Therapeutic Goods." ;
