doc:sec-54b-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "54B(1) Personal liability of an executive officer of a body corporate—" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) An executive officer of a body corporate commits an offence if: (a) the body corporate commits an offence against this Act covered by section 54BA; and (b) the officer knew that the offence would be committed; and (c) the officer was in a position to influence the conduct of the body in relation to the commission of the offence; and (d) the officer failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the commission of the offence. Note: An offence against this Act includes an offence against the regulations: see subsection 3(7)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "354"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54B(2) Personal liability of an executive officer of a body corporate—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-54b-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The maximum penalty for an offence against subsection (1) is: (a) the maximum penalty that a court could impose in respect of an individual for the offence committed by the body corporate; or (b) if the offence committed by the body corporate is an offence against subsection 41MN(10)—imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The maximum penalty for an offence against subsection (1) is: (a) the maximum penalty that a court could impose in respect of an individual for the offence committed by the body corporate; or (b) if the offence committed by the body corporate is an offence against subsection 41MN(10)—imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c982497a7430d06e5217d1b39e0558b2eeb8dfb9cc00cb6fe651fdd4402b6df6" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b ;
    cof:pageNumber "354"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Maximum penalty for an offence against subsection (1)" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
