concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Export certifications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary may issue export certification for goods for therapeutic use in humans, including certifications for the purposes of the World Health Organisation Certification Scheme on the Quality of Pharmaceutical Products Moving in International Commerce.  Chapter 7  Miscellaneous  Section 59 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for goods for therapeutic use in humans. (2A) The Secretary may issue export certification for vaping goods for use in humans that are not goods for which export certification may be issued under subsection (1). Note: Export certification for vaping goods that are for therapeutic use in humans may be issued under subsection (1). (2B) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for vaping goods for which export certification may be issued under subsection (2A). (3) Such fee as is prescribed is payable in respect of: (a) an application for a certification under this section; and (b) where an inspection of a manufacturing site is necessary for the purposes of the issue of a certification under this section—the inspection of that site." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Secretary may issue export certification for goods for therapeutic use in humans, including certifications for the purposes of the World Health Organisation Certification Scheme on the Quality of Pharmaceutical Products Moving in International Commerce.  Chapter 7  Miscellaneous  Section 59 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (2) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for goods for therapeutic use in humans. (2A) The Secretary may issue export certification for vaping goods for use in humans that are not goods for which export certification may be issued under subsection (1). Note: Export certification for vaping goods that are for therapeutic use in humans may be issued under subsection (1). (2B) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for vaping goods for which export certification may be issued under subsection (2A). (3) Such fee as is prescribed is payable in respect of: (a) an application for a certification under this section; and (b) where an inspection of a manufacturing site is necessary for the purposes of the issue of a certification under this section—the inspection of that site."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "da2ca4530f906c76ff51f7195cdbae8083d3bd829a37bfbc25ab09fcdd6e3398" ;
    cof:pageNumber "367"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2a ;
    cml:hasPart concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2b ;
