concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60A(2) New information on review—discretion to remit"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-60a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a person (the appellant) whose interests are affected by the decision requests the Minister to reconsider the decision, and lodges initial new information in support of that request, the Minister must either: (a) take that information into account when he or she reconsiders the decision; or (b) remit the matter to an authorised delegate for a fresh decision." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If a person (the appellant) whose interests are affected by the decision requests the Minister to reconsider the decision, and lodges initial new information in support of that request, the Minister must either: (a) take that information into account when he or she reconsiders the decision; or (b) remit the matter to an authorised delegate for a fresh decision."@en ;
