doc:sec-60a-ss-6a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "60A(6A) New information on review—discretion to remit" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6A) If: (a) the matter relates to a decision under section 41EC; and (b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and (c) the appellant has paid, as a further conformity assessment fee, the conformity assessment fee that the appellant would have to pay under section 41LA on making a new application for a conformity assessment certificate; the authorised delegate must make a decision under section 41EC, taking into account the initial new information or later new information (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application for a conformity assessment certificate had been made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "374"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60A(7) New information on review—discretion to remit"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-60a-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) To remove any doubt, the authorised delegate’s fresh decision is to be treated, for the purposes of subsequent applications of section 60 and this section, as a decision under Part 3-2, 3-2A or 4-4." ;
    skos:definition "(7) To remove any doubt, the authorised delegate’s fresh decision is to be treated, for the purposes of subsequent applications of section 60 and this section, as a decision under Part 3-2, 3-2A or 4-4."@en ;
