doc:sec-60a-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "60A(7) New information on review—discretion to remit" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) To remove any doubt, the authorised delegate’s fresh decision is to be treated, for the purposes of subsequent applications of section 60 and this section, as a decision under Part 3-2, 3-2A or 4-4." ;
    cof:pageNumber "374"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "60A(8) New information on review—discretion to remit"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-60a-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) In this section: authorised delegate means a delegate of the Secretary: (a) exercising a power to decide whether to register therapeutic goods; or (aa) exercising a power to decide whether to include a biological in the Register; or (b) exercising a power to decide whether to issue a conformity assessment certificate.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 7  Section 61 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 initial new information means information that: (a) was in existence at the time the decision referred to in subsection (1) was made; and (b) was not made available to the Secretary or authorised delegate for the purpose of making that decision; and (c) is relevant to that decision; and includes any opinions that are wholly or substantially based on such information (whether the opinions were formed before or after that decision was made). later new information means information that: (a) was in existence at the time the decision on reconsideration was made; and (b) was not made available to the Minister or delegate of the Minister for the purpose of making that decision; and (c) is relevant to that decision; and includes any opinions that are wholly or substantially based on such information (whether the opinions were formed before or after that decision was made)." ;
    skos:definition "(8) In this section: authorised delegate means a delegate of the Secretary: (a) exercising a power to decide whether to register therapeutic goods; or (aa) exercising a power to decide whether to include a biological in the Register; or (b) exercising a power to decide whether to issue a conformity assessment certificate.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 7  Section 61 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 initial new information means information that: (a) was in existence at the time the decision referred to in subsection (1) was made; and (b) was not made available to the Secretary or authorised delegate for the purpose of making that decision; and (c) is relevant to that decision; and includes any opinions that are wholly or substantially based on such information (whether the opinions were formed before or after that decision was made). later new information means information that: (a) was in existence at the time the decision on reconsideration was made; and (b) was not made available to the Minister or delegate of the Minister for the purpose of making that decision; and (c) is relevant to that decision; and includes any opinions that are wholly or substantially based on such information (whether the opinions were formed before or after that decision was made)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6d03ed07cd7b49ecbde9a6764bf00666f56d57ebc614c4b8fe44e5bfe24caaaa" ;
    values:partOf concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a ;
    cof:pageNumber "374"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines authorized delegate and conditions for new information." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
