    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In this section: therapeutic goods information means information in relation to therapeutic goods that is held by the Department and relates to the performance of the Department’s functions (including functions relating to the EC Mutual Recognition Agreement, the EFTA Mutual Recognition Agreement or the Australia-UK Mutual Recognition Agreement). vaping goods information means information in relation to vaping goods that is held by the Department and relates to the performance of the Department’s functions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "377"^^xsd:integer .

concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "61(2) Release of information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-61-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Secretary may: (a) release to the World Health Organisation therapeutic goods information relating to:  Chapter 7  Miscellaneous  Section 61 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (i) notifications concerning therapeutic goods the consumption or supply of which in Australia has been prohibited or severely restricted, or relating to the reasons for that action; or (ii) the licensing status of Australian manufacturers of therapeutic goods and their compliance with the manufacturing principles; or (iii) the content of reports to the Department concerning adverse effects of therapeutic goods; or (iv) the issue of, imposition of conditions on, or revocation of, conformity assessment certificates; for use in the development of policies relating to the regulation of therapeutic goods or for the provision of information to regulatory authorities of member countries of the World Health Organisation; or (b) release, in confidence, therapeutic goods information to the World Health Organisation, being information concerning proceedings of committees established under the regulations." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The Secretary may: (a) release to the World Health Organisation therapeutic goods information relating to:  Chapter 7  Miscellaneous  Section 61 Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 Compilation date: 05/09/2025 (i) notifications concerning therapeutic goods the consumption or supply of which in Australia has been prohibited or severely restricted, or relating to the reasons for that action; or (ii) the licensing status of Australian manufacturers of therapeutic goods and their compliance with the manufacturing principles; or (iii) the content of reports to the Department concerning adverse effects of therapeutic goods; or (iv) the issue of, imposition of conditions on, or revocation of, conformity assessment certificates; for use in the development of policies relating to the regulation of therapeutic goods or for the provision of information to regulatory authorities of member countries of the World Health Organisation; or (b) release, in confidence, therapeutic goods information to the World Health Organisation, being information concerning proceedings of committees established under the regulations."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "921fb311c11dd7500bee37650426b0a96bccb2bd398687deaa68c9efca17debc" ;
